e_margin_vs_hist":0.10703772313216067,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":6,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":66.7,"_gate_spread":-2.0440771709426846,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.9652041992503632,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":100.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.02056462803933607,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":26.5,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":0.020227615769743322,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":70.2,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0012903814922277138,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":12.5,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.03933040793109052,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":34.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.055760004,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":37.2,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Toast, Inc. operates a cloud-based digital technology platform for the restaurant industry in the United States, Ireland, India, and internationally. It offers a platform of software-as-a-service for restaurant operations and point of sale, such as Toast POS; Toast IQ, a conversational artificial intelligence; vendor management; multi-location management; kitchen display system; online ordering and delivery. It offers payroll and team management; inventory and supply chain tools; xtraCHEF by toast, a set of back-office tools for restaurants, including accounts payable automation, inventory management, ingredient price tracking, and recipe costing; financial technology solutions, including integrated payment processing, and restaurant-grade hardware. The company was formerly known as Opti Systems, Inc. and changed its name to Toast, Inc. in May 2012. Toast, Inc. was incorporated in 2011 and is headquartered in Boston, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Aman  Narang | Co-Founder, CEO & Director | Age 42 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 6K people. Revenue per employee of $947K ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers, with revenue growing 38%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $94K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $37K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Toast, Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $20.1B market cap on $6.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +31% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +4.5pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -193% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 22% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $608M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.93\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin -19.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.1%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 5.6% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 97% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.974903905268438},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $6.8M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Technology peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Technology peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Restaurant Partnerships Might Change The Case For Investing In Toast Stock (TOST)","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nyse-tost/toast/news/restaurant-partnerships-might-change-the-case-for-investing","date":"2026-11-14","timestamp":1794616728.238,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.935,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["product"]},{"title":"What Bernstein Thinks Has Already Played Out at Toast (TOST)","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/bernstein-thinks-already-played-toast-210936296.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794604176.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.421,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Toast, Inc. (TOST) Is a Trending Stock: Facts to Know Before Betting on It","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3028501/toast-inc-tost-is-a-trending-stock-facts-to-know-before-betting-on-it?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cmost_searched_stocks_v1-3028501","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794488403.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Here's Why Toast (TOST) is a Strong Growth Stock","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3028127/here-s-why-toast-tost-is-a-strong-growth-stock?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Czacks_education_growth_score-3028127","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794428226.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.71,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Toast Partners With Great Harvest to Support Bakery Expansion","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3029782/toast-partners-with-great-harvest-to-support-bakery-expansion?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Ccompany_news_finance_sector-3029782","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794590220.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.778,"tier":1,"